    "publishedAt": "2026-11-02",
    "summary": "As an external graphics solution, the XG Core powers the GPU through the PCIe slot without needing external GPU PCIe power connectors. The differences in frequency also correlate with power consumption. The Navi 44 XTLP in the XG Core solution is rated for just 75 W, while the desktop GPU is designed for a 140 W power draw and requires an external GPU power connector. This aggressive power limit necessitates lower clock speeds to maintain stability and thermal performance within its compact chassis, which measures roughly 114 × 117 × 39 mm.",
